# Build outputs. `*.exe` covers the Windows-style `go build -o <tool>.exe`
# the tool READMEs document; the plain `go build ./cmd/<tool>` a macOS/Linux
# checkout runs writes an *extensionless* binary named after the package
# directory into the repo root, which nothing else here catches — an 11MB
# `gate` once rode into a commit on `git add -A`. Each name is root-anchored
# with a leading `/` so it matches only the build output: an unanchored `gate`
# would also match the `cmd/gate/` source tree.
#
# `cmd/local` and `cmd/driverstate` are deliberately absent. `local/` and
# `driverstate/` are tracked packages at the repo root, so `go build` refuses
# to write over them ("build output already exists and is a directory") and
# there is no stray binary to catch. Adding `/local` here would not fix a leak;
# it would make git ignore new files inside that package. CI's `hygiene` job
# keeps this list in step with `cmd/`, including that exemption.
*.exe
/ci-classify-eval
/codexguard
/console
/custody
/dispatch
/escalate
/eval
/flare
/gate
/org
/org-mcp
/review
/reviewfindings
/runway
/stubgate
/tracelens
/triage-advisory
/triage-floor
/workbench-mcp

# Nested-module build output: cmd/gate/docs/features/ci-classify/eval/build is
# its own module, so `go build` there writes beside its go.mod, not at the root.
/cmd/gate/docs/features/ci-classify/eval/build/s2build

coverage.out
.demo-state/

.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials*
secrets/

# agent-runtime / session state — keep out of a public repo
.claude/
.huddle/
.playwright-mcp/
.gate-executor-keys/
.github/actions/gate-executor/gate
/fleet
